{%- comment -%}
  Artwork origination add-on — an opt-in £20 line item added alongside the bottle.

  Sells the label guide's OVERPRINT path only: a logo, crest or graphic added to our
  existing canvas label. The guide's other path ("a completely custom label") is
  deliberately NOT sold here — its own card says "that's a job for a chat, not a
  checkout". Don't let the copy here drift into promising a from-scratch design.

  Price and variant BOTH come from the `fee_product` setting, so the page cannot
  advertise one price and charge another. The label guide reads the same product.

  How the inputs behave, and why:
    • The checkbox carries `properties[Artwork] = Yes`, so even WITHOUT JavaScript a
      tick reaches the order as a flag you can act on — no fee is added, but you see
      the request rather than losing it silently.
    • The textarea ships `disabled` and is enabled by JS only when the box is ticked,
      so nothing strays into the cart from a panel nobody opened.

  Inputs sit OUTSIDE the <form> (Dawn keeps the form in buy-buttons), so every one
  needs form="{{ product_form_id }}" — the same association the variant picker and
  quantity use.

  Usage: {% render 'wb-artwork-addon', block: block, product_form_id: product_form_id %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign fee_product = block.settings.fee_product
  assign fee_variant = fee_product.first_available_variant
  if fee_variant == blank
    assign fee_variant = fee_product.variants.first
  endif
-%}

{%- if fee_variant != blank -%}
  <div
    class="wb-artwork-addon wb-bottle-form"
    data-wb-artwork-addon
    data-fee-variant-id="{{ fee_variant.id }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <div class="wb-artwork-addon__row">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        id="wb-artwork-optin-{{ block.id }}"
        class="wb-artwork-addon__checkbox"
        name="properties[Artwork]"
        value="Yes"
        data-wb-artwork-optin
        form="{{ product_form_id }}"
      >
      <label class="wb-artwork-addon__label" for="wb-artwork-optin-{{ block.id }}">
        <span class="wb-artwork-addon__heading">
          {{- block.settings.heading | default: 'Add your own artwork to the label' -}}
        </span>
        <span class="wb-artwork-addon__price">
          +{% render 'wb-money', amount: fee_variant.price %}
        </span>
      </label>
    </div>

    <div class="wb-artwork-addon__panel" data-wb-artwork-panel hidden>
      <label for="wb-artwork-brief-{{ block.id }}">Tell us what you have in mind</label>
      <textarea
        id="wb-artwork-brief-{{ block.id }}"
        name="properties[Artwork details]"
        rows="3"
        disabled
        data-wb-artwork-brief
        {%- comment -%}
          Kept short on purpose: .wb-bottle-form sets textareas to 18px, and at 375px
          a longer placeholder is clipped mid-word inside three rows.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        placeholder="Your idea, and whether you have artwork ready."
        form="{{ product_form_id }}"
      ></textarea>

      <p class="wb-artwork-addon__note">
        {{ block.settings.note | default: "Send your artwork to info@whiskyblender.com after ordering. We'll email you to get started, send a proof, and won't print until you're happy with it." }}
        {%- if block.settings.guide_url != blank %}
          <a href="{{ block.settings.guide_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the label guide</a>.
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script src="{{ 'wb-artwork-addon.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
